<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Italian Republic (1802–1805)</h1><p class="st-meta">1802 CE – 1805 CE · capital Milan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Napoleon's Italian Republic, the first state to bear the name Italy, governed for him from Milan by Francesco Melzi d'Eril.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consulta-of-lyon">Consulta of Lyon</a> in January 1802, Italian delegates of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisalpine-republic">Cisalpine Republic</a> accepted a new constitution and elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> as president. The republic was renamed Italian, a symbolic step for supporters of national unity.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, while Vice-President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-melzi-deril">Francesco Melzi d'Eril</a> governed in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a>, building an efficient administration, reforming finances, introducing conscription and making a concordat with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> in 1803. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prefect">prefects</a> followed the French model, and the republic's army fought in Napoleon's campaigns.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> became emperor of the French, he turned the republic into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-italy-napoleonic">Kingdom of Italy (Napoleonic)</a> in March 1805 and crowned himself king in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1802 CE – 1805 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.56%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1802 CE – 1805 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Milan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Napoleon Bonaparte, Francesco Melzi d'Eril</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Repubblica Italiana (Napoleonic)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1804&amp;focus=italian-republic-1802-1805" aria-label="Italian Republic (1802–1805) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4983 667 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Italian Republic (1802–1805) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5303 923L5218 830M5303 923L5054 728M5303 923L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0M5054 728h0M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5303 923h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5303 923h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1804&amp;focus=italian-republic-1802-1805">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
